# RiverLine SDD — production Caddy config (docker-compose.prod.yml).
# Build spec §2.8: "Vercel or a single VPS with Caddy for automatic HTTPS.
# HTTPS is non-negotiable: iOS will not grant camera or geolocation
# permissions to insecure origins."
#
# {$SITE_ADDRESS} is set via the `SITE_ADDRESS` env var
# (.env.production.example). Caddy's automatic HTTPS already does the right
# thing for both cases with zero extra directives:
#   - A real public hostname (e.g. flood.noblesville.example.gov) ->
#     Caddy requests a real certificate from Let's Encrypt automatically on
#     first request. Requires ports 80+443 reachable from the internet for
#     the ACME HTTP-01 challenge.
#   - "localhost" (the default, used for local/self-host testing without a
#     public domain) -> not a publicly resolvable/ACME-eligible name, so
#     Caddy transparently falls back to its own internal CA and serves a
#     self-signed certificate instead. Real HTTPS, just not
#     browser-trusted without importing Caddy's local root CA — fine for
#     the docker-compose prove-out documented in docs/deploy/self-host.md,
#     wrong for a real pilot jurisdiction (set SITE_ADDRESS to the real
#     domain there).
{$SITE_ADDRESS:localhost} {
	encode gzip

	reverse_proxy app:3000
}
